Your control plane is in good shape now. All three etcd pods, API servers, controller managers, and schedulers are running. The `NotReady` status is exactly because `cni: none` is still configured, so Cilium is the next functional dependency.

The `etcdctl` failure is separate. This part tells us what happened:

```text
/bin/sh: line 1: --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379: No such file or directory
```

That means:

```bash
ETCDCTL=$(find /var/lib/rancher/rke2/data -type f -name etcdctl | head -1)
```

returned **nothing**, so the shell effectively tried to execute:

```bash
--endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379
```

### First, confirm whether `etcdctl` exists on the host

Run:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a 'find /var/lib/rancher/rke2 -type f -name "etcdctl" -o -name "etcdctl*" 2>/dev/null'
```

Also:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a 'find /var/lib/rancher/rke2/data -type f -path "*/bin/*" | grep -E "/etcd|/etcdctl" || true'
```

If you get something like:

```text
/var/lib/rancher/rke2/data/<hash>/bin/etcdctl
```

then use that exact path.

But newer RKE2 layouts do not always expose `etcdctl` directly on the host. In that case, use the running etcd process.

### Reliable method: use the etcd process root

First find the etcd PID:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a 'pgrep -af "etcd"'
```

Then locate `etcdctl` inside the container filesystem:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a '
PID=$(pgrep -f "/usr/local/bin/etcd" | head -1)
echo "ETCD PID=$PID"
find /proc/$PID/root -type f -name etcdctl 2>/dev/null | head
'
```

You will probably see something similar to:

```text
/proc/75133/root/usr/local/bin/etcdctl
```

Then run:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a '
PID=$(pgrep -f "/usr/local/bin/etcd" | head -1)
ETCDCTL=/proc/$PID/root/usr/local/bin/etcdctl

$ETCDCTL \
  --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 \
  --cacert=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-ca.crt \
  --cert=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-client.crt \
  --key=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-client.key \
  member list -w table
'
```

You want three rows, corresponding to:

```text
master01
master02
master03
```

Then check endpoint health:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a '
PID=$(pgrep -f "/usr/local/bin/etcd" | head -1)
ETCDCTL=/proc/$PID/root/usr/local/bin/etcdctl

$ETCDCTL \
  --endpoints=https://10.174.161.22:2379,https://10.174.161.23:2379,https://10.174.161.24:2379 \
  --cacert=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-ca.crt \
  --cert=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-client.crt \
  --key=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-client.key \
  endpoint health -w table
'
```

And finally:

```bash
ansible master01 \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  -b \
  -m shell \
  -a '
PID=$(pgrep -f "/usr/local/bin/etcd" | head -1)
ETCDCTL=/proc/$PID/root/usr/local/bin/etcdctl

$ETCDCTL \
  --endpoints=https://10.174.161.22:2379,https://10.174.161.23:2379,https://10.174.161.24:2379 \
  --cacert=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-ca.crt \
  --cert=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-client.crt \
  --key=/var/lib/rancher/rke2/server/tls/etcd/server-client.key \
  endpoint status -w table
'
```

You want:

```text
3 endpoints
all healthy
one leader
two followers
same/similar raft index
no learner stuck
no errors
```

At that point I would consider the **RKE2 control-plane bootstrap complete**.

Then proceed immediately to Cilium, because your current node readiness output already proves the only blocker is:

```text
NetworkPluginNotReady
cni plugin not initialized
```

So the sequence is now:

